"fact_7bde8096ae5e910bb83292d4\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s40\",\"s21\",\"s13\",\"s5\",\"s20\",\"s39\",\"s32\",\"s12\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s30\",\"s31\",\"s4\",\"s3\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user describes multiple recent community event experiences: a book swap that became overwhelming and disheartening (s3-s5), a successful author interview event that was exciting and worthwhile (s12-s13), a reading marathon for charity that fostered community and enjoyment (s30-s32), a regular library volunteering schedule that is fulfilling (s39-s40), and a community buying group that was less engaging and disappointing (s20-s22, s47-s48). These sources collectively support a mixed summary of recent experiences and feelings about planning and participating in community events.\",\"variable\":\"event_experience\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t0\"},{\"id\":\"fact_5b8d34030265c4dc1076dcc0\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s40\",\"s21\",\"s13\",\"s5\",\"s20\",\"s39\",\"s32\",\"s12\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s30\",\"s31\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s49\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user describes multiple past community involvement experiences. Positive: a reading marathon for charity (s30-s32) where they felt a real sense of community; an author interview event (s12-s13) that was awe-inspiring and made preparation worthwhile; and regular library volunteering (s39-s40) that is rewarding and fosters literacy. Negative: a book swap (s3-s5) that became overwhelming and disheartening; and a buying group (s20-s22, s47-s49) that lacked engagement and felt stagnant. These together show a pattern of valuing literary community activities but being sensitive to organizational complexity and group dynamics.\",\"variable\":\"community_values\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t1\"},{\"id\":\"fact_a4d2332abe8b13e534342988\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s40\",\"s21\",\"s13\",\"s5\",\"s20\",\"s39\",\"s32\",\"s12\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s30\",\"s31\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s49\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user's own statements across multiple conversations describe both positive and negative experiences with community event planning. The positive experiences (author interview, reading marathon, library volunteering) show successful and rewarding engagement, while the negative experiences (book swap, buying group) highlight stress, overwhelm, and disengagement. These are all current reflections on past activities, providing a comprehensive picture of the user's current constraints and feelings about continuing community event involvement.\",\"variable\":\"current_constraints\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t2\"},{\"id\":\"fact_adb0a5ba9199174dd3a51835\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s40\",\"s21\",\"s13\",\"s5\",\"s20\",\"s39\",\"s32\",\"s12\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s30\",\"s31\",\"s4\",\"s3\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user's own statements across multiple conversations describe both positive and negative experiences with community event planning and organizing. The book swap (s3-s5) was overwhelming and disheartening. The author interview (s12-s13) was exciting and rewarding. The charity reading marathon (s30-s32) was a positive community experience. The library volunteering (s39-s40) is fulfilling. The buying group (s20-s22, s47-s48) was less engaging and stagnant. These are all direct user statements, not assistant suggestions.\",\"variable\":\"planning_preferences\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t3\"},{\"id\":\"fact_634e1f2d3064d07498160ba4\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"It sounds like you might be feeling a bit overwhelmed or finding the process less enjoyable than before. If the structured planning is becoming tedious, perhaps focusing on more spontaneous or informal engagement within the community could be a refreshing change. Consider activities that require less meticulous planning and more personal interaction. How do you feel about trying something like that?\",\"source_ids\":[\"s40\",\"s21\",\"s13\",\"s5\",\"s20\",\"s39\",\"s32\",\"s12\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s30\",\"s31\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s49\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{\"event_experience\":1,\"community_values\":1,\"current_constraints\":1,\"planning_preferences\":1},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user's history shows mixed experiences: overwhelming book swap (s3-s5), disappointing buying group (s20-s22, s47-s49), but rewarding author interview (s12-s13), reading marathon (s30-s32), and library volunteering (s39-s40). The user values community but is sensitive to complexity and disengagement. Option (c) directly addresses the overwhelm and suggests less structured, more personal engagement, which aligns with the user's positive experiences (reading marathon, library volunteering) and avoids the pitfalls of the negative ones (book swap, buying group). This best fits the user's current constraints and preferences.\",\"variable\":\"response\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",105,458,\"User: Organizing the book swap seemed like a delightful idea initially, but as I delved into the planning stage, the complexities started to unfold in ways I hadn't anticipated. The thoughts of coordinating different genres, managing people's varying schedules, and ensuring there were enough participants to make it worthwhile all became overwhelming. \",\"user\",[42]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",458,800,\"I found myself trying to devise a system that would work for everyone involved, but with each attempt, I felt more and more stressed rather than excited. The logistics of gathering different books, sorting them by category, and then figuring out how to distribute them fairly seemed like a task that was becoming more daunting by the minute. \",\"user\",[42]],[\"s5\",\"d1\",800,1014,\"Ultimately, it seemed that I was investing too much time and energy into something that was supposed to be a fun community experience, which left me feeling disheartened about pursuing similar events in the future.\",\"user\",[42]],[\"s12\",\"d2\",105,457,\"User: Lastly, I successfully conducted an engaging interview with a well-known author, which led to an exciting community event. The experience of speaking with someone who has had such a profound impact on the literary world was awe-inspiring. I learned so much not only about their writing process but also about their personal journey as an author. \",\"user\",[67]],[\"s13\",\"d2\",457,640,\"It felt like stepping into a world that was both familiar and completely new. Seeing the immediate excitement it generated in the community really made all the preparation worthwhile.\",\"user\",[67]],[\"s20\",\"d3\",107,359,\"User: Lastly, I joined a community-based buying group, but I found it less engaging than I anticipated. Initially, I was excited about the idea of being part of a collective, where people share and collaborate on purchases to benefit from bulk buying. \",\"user\",[138]],[\"s21\",\"d3\",359,728,\"I imagined engaging discussions with like-minded individuals about our shared interests and needs, perhaps even discovering new products or services I had never considered before. However, as time went on, I noticed that the interactions weren't as dynamic or fulfilling as I had hoped; there wasn't much enthusiasm in the conversations, and it felt somewhat stagnant. \",\"user\",[138]],[\"s22\",\"d3\",728,874,\"Additionally, I realized that the group didn't have a clear focus or direction, which contributed to my sense of disengagement and disappointment.\",\"user\",[138]],[\"s30\",\"d4\",105,450,\"User: I even joined a reading marathon for charity! It was a structured event that promoted community involvement, where participants from diverse backgrounds came together to share their love for reading. The organization of the event was meticulous, with schedules, reading lists, and even group discussions planned to enhance our experience. \",\"user\",[63]],[\"s31\",\"d4\",450,761,\"I witnessed how everyone was not just focused on individual achievements, but also on encouraging one another and celebrating our collective progress. It was refreshing to see people's eyes light up when they talked about their favorite books, creating bonds that seemed to transcend the pages we were turning. \",\"user\",[63]],[\"s32\",\"d4\",761,910,\"Ultimately, I found a real sense of community in the challenge, as we all cheered each other on and exchanged thoughts about our literary adventures.\",\"user\",[63]],[\"s39\",\"d5\",107,396,\"User: On a positive note, I started a regular volunteering schedule at the local library. It's been a great way to engage with the community and help out with outreach programs. Every week, I look forward to connecting with people of all ages who share a passion for reading and learning. \",\"user\",[147]],[\"s40\",\"d5\",396,630,\"There’s something special about watching children’s faces light up when they discover a new book or hear a story being read aloud. It’s rewarding to think that I’m playing a small part in fostering a love for literacy in my community.\",\"user\",[147]],[\"s47\",\"d6\",107,342,\"User: I thought being part of a community-based buying group would be a great way to connect with others who share similar interests and values, especially since it promised the potential for bulk discounts on items we frequently use. \",\"user\",[140]],[\"s48\",\"d6\",342,721,\"However, after attending a few meetings, I r